miu_0.5.problem:
Define $\mathcal{A}$ as the collection of all polynomials involving three variables $t, u, v$ with coefficients that are integers. Let $\mathcal{B}$ be the subset of $\mathcal{A}$ consisting of polynomials that can be represented in the form:
\begin{align*}
(t + u + v)P(t, u, v) + (tu + uv + vt)Q(t, u, v) + tuvR(t, u, v)
\end{align*}
where $P, Q, R$ are elements of $\mathcal{A}$. Determine the least non-negative integer $m$ such that $t^a u^b v^c$ belongs to $\mathcal{B}$ for all non-negative integers $a, b, c$ with $a + b + c$ being at least $m$.

miu_0.9.problem:
Consider the assemblage $\mathcal{M}$ representing all polynomials involving three symbolic entities $t, u, v$ possessing coefficients that are numerals from ℤ. Define the collection $\mathcal{N}$ as the subset within $\mathcal{M}$ composed of polynomials expressible in the format:
\begin{align*}
(t + u + v)F(t, u, v) + (tu + uv + vt)G(t, u, v) + tuvH(t, u, v)
\end{align*}
where $F, G, H$ belong to $\mathcal{M}$. Determine the smallest non-negative whole number $m$ for which $t^a u^b v^c$ is an element of $\mathcal{N}$ for all non-negative numerals $a, b, c$ fulfilling the condition $a + b + c \geq m$.
